- Story & Context: The keepers at Cape Kvitøya stopped broadcasting to the ships and started listening to the return signals, which had become a repetitive, rhythmic clicking language. Kjetil recorded the sound of the ice shifting against the lighthouse foundation and layered it over the clicks, believing it was a map to a hidden harbor. Nobody ever arrived to claim the signal, but the recording remains the most mythologized track in the scene. "We traded the maps for a rhythm that never ends."
